    "https://www.hsc.edu/human-resources/job-openings": {
      "title": "Careers and Job Openings",
      "description": "Job Openings Skip to Content Visit Apply Give You are here: Home Human Resources Job Openings Careers and Job Openings Human Resources Benefits Employee Handbook HR Forms Leave Job Openings Organizational Charts Contact HR Why Work at H-SC Hampden-Sydney College is a selective liberal arts institution with a distinctive mission: to form good men and good citizens in an atmosphere of sound learning. As one of only three private liberal arts colleges in the United States dedicated exclusively to the education of men, the College combines a rich tradition with an unwavering commitment to academic excellence, leadership, and character. Our picturesque 1,300-acre campus features hiking and biking trails, a Frisbee golf course, an adventure high ropes and zip line course, and numerous opportunities to enjoy the outdoors. Just minutes from historic downtown Farmville, employees enjoy access to local restaurants, breweries, art galleries, the Moton Museum, the High Bridge Trail, and several nearby state parks. Richmond, Lynchburg, Charlottesville, Washington, D.C., and the Blue Ridge Mountains are all within easy reach, offering abundant cultural, recreational, and professional opportunities. As a community, we are dedicated to the goal of building a culturally diverse staff committed to working in a multicultural environment and strongly encourage applications from women and minoritized groups. Hampden-Sydney College values diversity, prohibits discrimination, and is committed to equal opportunity for all employees and applicants for employment. Seeking qualified candidates for the following Faculty Openings Administration Openings How to Apply Online submission is available from each job description.  You may also print and mail your application to: Hampden-Sydney College Human Resources | P.O. Box 25 Hampden Sydney, VA 23943 Application for Employment (.pdf format) Application for Employment (.doc format) Why Work at Hampden-Sydney College? At Hampden-Sydney College, employees are not just staff members—they are partners in shaping future leaders, and we are committed to recognizing, rewarding, and supporting our employees in every aspect of their lives. Find out more about our generous compensation programs. Working at H-SC Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The Annual Fire and Security Report includes campus security information, campus fire statistics, safety procedures, and provides statistics for criminal and disciplinary offenses. The report is provided annually in compliance with the Clery Act and the Higher Education Opportunity Act (HEOA). A hard copy of the Annual Security and Fire Report and/or a copy of the Fire Log are maintained at the Hampden-Sydney College Department of Public Safety and Police and will be provided upon request. Hampden-Sydney College Annual Security and Fire Report is available the Public Safety and Police website. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Harassment and Discrimination Policy As a community, we are dedicated to the goal of building a culturally diverse staff committed to working in a multicultural environment and strongly encourage applications from women and minoritized groups. Hampden-Sydney College values diversity, prohibits discrimination, and is committed to equal opportunity for all employees and applicants for employment. Every College staff member, faculty member, and student has the right to work and study in an environment free from discrimination and harassment and should be treated with dignity and respect. The College prohibits discrimination and harassment against applicants for employment or admission, students, faculty, or staff on the basis of the following protected categories: race, color, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity and gender expression), religion, age, national or ethnic origin, family medical or genetic information, disability, familial, or veteran status, or any other category protected by state or local law, in the operation of its educational programs, community social activities or programs. Harassment and Discrimination Policy Human Resources Benefits Employee Handbook HR Forms Leave Job Openings Organizational Charts Contact HR Why Work at H-SC A-Z Index Campus Map Campus Store Directories Emergencies Events Human Resources Library News Policies Tiger Web Virtual Tour Visit Apply Give Hampden Sydney, VA 23943 (434) 223-6000 Contact the College Privacy Policy © 2026 Hampden-Sydney College Search Academics Majors & Minors Academic Opportunities Rhetoric Program Student Research Global Education Career Center Academic Services Admission & Financial Aid Apply Request Information Schedule Visit Financial Aid Accepted Students Tuition & Fees Student Life Campus Living Honor & Conduct What to Do Campus Resources Campus Culture Civic Engagement About H-SC Why H-SC Facts & Figures History Offices and Services Administration Visit Apply Give Campus News Catch up on the latest campus news and find out what's happening at Hampden-Sydney College. News Index Quick Links Alumni Current Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Family Academic Centers Athletics Campus Store Campus Map College Events Directories Employment Library Support a Student Tiger Web Search"
