    "https://www.hsc.edu/academics/career-center": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Career Center Skip to Content Visit Apply Give You are here: Home Academics Career Center Career Center Academics Majors & Minors Academic Requirements Career Preparation Choosing a Major Find Your Passion Academic Opportunities Cooperative Programs Summer Term Student Research Summer Research Summer Research Application Summer Research Opportunities Research Fellows Student Research Stories Career Center Students TigerWorks Internships Internship Scholarships Fellowships Employers Employer Partnerships Alumni Graduate Outcomes Academic Services Academic Success Advising Major & Minor Checklists Student Resources Success Seminar Disability Services Accommodations, Responsibility, Assessment Disability Documentation Emotional Support Animal Policy Language Substitution Math Substitution Mobility Cart Note-taking Policy Service Animal Policy Welcome! From resumes and cover letters to networking and interviewing tips, the Career Center offers career coaching sessions, workshops and other resources to help students navigate the journey from exploring a career to finding a job. Visit the Career Center, attend an event, connect with fellow Tigers, or browse our career resources in Handshake. Career Center Staff Director of the Career Center, Scott Crawford scrawford@hsc.edu | (434) 223-6325 Associate Director of Career Education, Patrick Jourdain ’88, M.S. pjourdain@hsc.edu Assistant Director of Experiential Programs and Student Employment, Ashley Crute acrute@hsc.edu Assistant Director for Programming and Partnerships, Emilee Farabaugh efarabaugh@hsc.edu Assistant Director of Alumni and Employer Relations, Emily Sadler esadler@hsc.edu OFFICE HOURS: Monday-Friday | 9 am-5 pm and Monday-Wednesday | 7 pm-9 pm Contact Career Center Gilmer Hall, 102, Hampden-Sydney College (434) 223-6106 career@hsc.edu How can we help you? Students From resumes and cover letters to networking and interviewing tips, Career Services helps students navigate the journey from exploring a career to finding a job with coaching sessions, workshops, and other resources. Let's Go Employers The Career Center is dedicated to supporting and cultivating relationships between our students and employers by hosting career events and partnerships, and helping you hire your next employee. Let's Go Alumni The Career Center is dedicated to supporting alumni and building success in whatever path they choose to pursue with career advice, resources, recruitment opportunities, and alumni connections. Let's Go Hampden-Sydney Connects Brotherhood in Action: Connect with other Tigers Leverage one of the best alumni networks in the nation to discover job and internship opportunities, foster lifelong relationships, and enhance your personal reach and presence. Activate your account in minutes - and tap into the power of our lifelong Brotherhood. H-SConnects TigerWorks Student employment at Hampden-Sydney TigerWorks is Hampden-Sydney College’s on-campus student employment program for both institutional and federal work-study. Let us help you find a campus job! TigerWorks Graduate Outcomes We know our graduates do well after leaving the Hill. Our outcomes prove that. Hampden-Sydney College is committed to student success beyond graduation, and the results are in: o ur graduates are not only successful, but they start their careers earning more than their peers from other institutions, and they'll do it with support from the second best alumni network in the nation. Considered a best value college for its return on investment, H-SC ranks among the top 10 colleges for career preparation according to The Princeton Review and The Wall Street Journal . Graduate Outcomes Alumni Career Stories They say \"you can do anything with a degree from Hampden-Sydney.\" Our alumni prove that! From pediatricians and philanthropists, to marketing executives and athletic coaches, here's what you can do with an H-SC degree. Alumni Story Index Join Handshake Finding a job and building a career can be daunting. Handshake is here to help. Whether you're looking for an internship, full-time job or don't know where to begin, you can use Handshake to discover employers and opportunities, submit applications, find career education resources, and connect with alumni at Hampden-Sydney College events. Login to Handshake Need help accessing Handshake? Please log in and complete your profile. The more information we know about you, the better we can communicate with you specifically about internships and jobs in the field and location of your choice. You may opt for the “Single Sign-On” (SSO) option, and enjoy safe, simple access to the platform from any secure identity or device. Handshake HELP How do I access Handshake? Sign in to Handshake with your Hampden-Sydney user ID and password. We encourage you to complete your profile in order to get the best job recommendations, messages, and events that matter to you. Tips Handshake has a number of tutorials and a great support team. Below are quick resources to help you get started with Handshake. Help Center (support articles, quick videos, content for students) Video Library (student overview, etc.) What you'll see when you first log in What do I do if some of my profile information is incorrect? Much of your information is brought over from our databases, which comes straight from the Registrar. We recommend connecting with the Registrar's office to be sure your information is correct. For additional questions, please contact career@hsc.edu . How do I find events and information sessions in Handshake? Information sessions and career workshops can be found by clicking \"Events\" from the left hand menu. Career fairs can be found by clicking \"Fairs\" from the lefthand menu. Login to Handshake Stay Connected on Social Media Connect with the Career Center on social media and follow us to get the most current information about what's happening! H-SC Official LinkedIn H-SC Alumni Association LinkedIn Careers on Instagram Careers on Facebook Contact Career Center Gilmer Hall, 102, Hampden-Sydney College (434) 223-6106 career@hsc.edu A-Z Index Campus Map Campus Store Directories Emergencies Events Human Resources Library News Policies Tiger Web Virtual Tour Visit Apply Give Hampden Sydney, VA 23943 (434) 223-6000 Contact the College Privacy Policy © 2026 Hampden-Sydney College Search Academics Majors & Minors Academic Opportunities Rhetoric Program Student Research Global Education Career Center Academic Services Admission & Financial Aid Apply Request Information Schedule Visit Financial Aid Accepted Students Tuition & Fees Student Life Campus Living Honor & Conduct What to Do Campus Resources Campus Culture Civic Engagement About H-SC Why H-SC Facts & Figures History Offices and Services Administration Visit Apply Give Campus News Catch up on the latest campus news and find out what's happening at Hampden-Sydney College. News Index Quick Links Alumni Current Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Family Academic Centers Athletics Campus Store Campus Map College Events Directories Employment Library Support a Student Tiger Web Search"
    }
